          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "Dense, pale yellow wood from trees of the genus Buxus. Although difficult to carve, the wood has excellent dimensional stability and is very wear resistant. The hard, fine-grain wood is often used for printing blocks, rulers, mallets, architects scales, slide rules, modeling tools, musical instruments, engravings, inlays, small decorative items, and game pieces. [Source: Getty AAT]"
    }
  ],
